================================================================================
## Merge origin/0.10.0 into the incremental-materialization branch
================================================================================

Context: `origin/0.10.0` (61 commits, 504 files) brings the graph backend
split — `GraphDBBackend.py` → the `back/core/graphdb/interfaces/` package
(`GraphBackend`, `MaterializedGraphBackend`, `VirtualBackend`, the
`GraphBuilder` / `GraphHealthProbe` / `GraphProvisioner` / `GraphSimulation`
capabilities vended by `GraphDBFactory`), the delta modules renamed and split
(`DeltaFlatStore` → `ReadStore` + `MaterializedStore` + `ViewStore`,
`DeltaBase` → `Base`, `DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline` → `BuildPipeline`,
`DeltaOverviewStats` → `OverviewStats`), the lakebase modules renamed
(`LakebaseFlatStore` → `FlatStore`, `LakebaseBase` → `Base`,
`LakebaseGraphProvisioner` → `InstanceProvisioner`), an import-boundary
architecture test, the what-if simulation feature, the "Graph" workspace
name, deploy defaults on instance `10x` and `sql`-only app scopes, the
ontology-pitfalls removal and dependency floors — on top of this branch's
207 commits of incremental / microbatch / realtime materialization. 36 files
conflicted; four reviewers (docs, mcp-server, translators, data quality) and
one store port (delta) ran in parallel on disjoint files, the core merge was
done by hand.

Resolution, by area:

1. Core merge (by hand): `GraphDBFactory.py` keeps our materialization-mode
   resolution and the Neo4j store's inferred ledger with their `Store` name,
   builders, probes, `classify_store`; `delta/__init__.py`, `lakebase/__init__.py`
   export both sides' classes under the new names; `_companion_ddl.py` keeps our
   asserted / live DDL and their simulation DDL; `delta/BuildPipeline.py` uses
   `MaterializedStore`; `_build_pipeline.py` keeps our compute-once / MERGE
   fallback / `SyncPlan` path and gains their `_delta_write_builder` /
   `_lakebase_builder` helpers the auto-merged call sites use;
   `schedule/build.py` keeps our tick (`_tick_modes`, `_tick_sync_plan`);
   `dtwin.py` keeps our routes; `pyproject.toml`, `databricks.yml` (scopes:
   `sql` only), both `uv.lock`s take theirs; `GraphDBBackend.py` is removed and
   its `_sql_relation` docstring note lives in `interfaces/GraphBackend.py`.
2. Delta store port (reviewer): our Lakehouse//RT fast path (`_sql_relation`
   via `GraphReadRelation`, `execute_query(bounded=)`, `RT_FALLBACK_MARKERS`,
   the build-warehouse fallback) lives in `ReadStore`; our companion rebuild
   improvements in `MaterializedStore`; `expand_and_fetch_subgraph`'s
   recursive-CTE assembly extracted to `ReadStore._expansion_sql` (Extract
   Method: the merged method was 114 LOC).
3. Translators (reviewer): `SparqlTranslator` keeps our incremental SQL and
   `TripleSQLAssembler` plus their collapsed-UC-FQN rewrite; `SWRLSQLTranslator`
   keeps our negation / incremental filters and takes their dialect-aware
   builtin compile (`SWRLBuiltinRegistry.sql_template_for`: Postgres `RLIKE`,
   `DATEDIFF`, guarded `::float8` casts) — the merged class crossed the 800-LOC
   ceiling, so the builtin compile is extracted to
   `swrl/SWRLSQLBuiltinFilters.py` (`resolve_arg`, `build`; Extract Class) and
   our superseded `SWRLSQLBuiltinFilters` string-rewrite module is gone;
   `tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_builtin_defects.py` asserts the guarded
   Postgres cast instead of `DOUBLE PRECISION`.
4. Data quality / misc (reviewer): `DataQualitySnapshot`, `models.py`,
   `agents/tools/mapping.py` take their factory / builder wiring; tests patch
   `delta.Base.create_databricks_client` and `ViewStore`.
5. mcp-server (reviewer): theirs (both sides had implemented the same two MCP
   fixes); docs (reviewer): both sides merged, README "What's new in 0.10.0"
   folds our 0.9.2 bullets, "Knowledge Graph" → "Graph".
6. Rename sweep: 23 non-conflicted files still naming the old modules now
   import `delta.Base`, `delta.MaterializedStore`, `lakebase.Base`,
   `lakebase.FlatStore` (aliased where our identifiers stay), tests patch the
   owning modules (`MaterializedStore.materialize`, `lakebase.Builder.Builder.
   resolve_sync_uc_fallback_catalog`, `neo4j.Store.Store`).
7. Import boundary (`tests/units/architecture/test_backend_import_boundary.py`):
   the materialization orchestration (`back/objects/digitaltwin/build/`,
   `back/objects/registry/schedule/`) is engine-aware by design and may import
   the engines' mechanics; a second test forbids it the concrete stores and
   backend roots. Accordingly: `TwinLiveServing`, `TwinRealtimeStream` and the
   scheduled tick ask `GraphDBFactory.classify_store(store) == "lakebase"`
   instead of `isinstance(store, LakebaseBase)`; `TwinIncrementalStatus` and
   `TwinLiveServing` get the sync fallback catalog from the Lakebase `Builder`;
   `TwinLakebaseSync` imports `SYNC_TABLE_MODES` from the `lakebase` package
   (now exported); `dtwin.py` and `TwinRealtimeStream` take the caller's
   build-warehouse client from the new `GraphDBFactory.build_warehouse_client`
   (one copy of what both duplicated); `CohortBuilder` and `ReasoningService`
   call the new interface method `GraphBackend.record_inferred(triples)`
   (default no-op; the Neo4j `Store` forwards to its ledger) instead of
   importing `InferredTripleLedger`; `classify_store` keys on the Lakebase
   hat root `Base` (every Lakebase store and test double derives from it).
   `.cursor/07-project-conventions.mdc` states the carve-out.
8. Size baseline: resolved as a true merge — the union of both parents'
   entries, then `python -m tests.units.architecture.ratchet` (shrink-only)
   dropped the stale ones; the two offenders the union created were fixed
   (items 2 and 3), not baselined.
9. docs/incremental-materialization.md names the new store classes.
10. Lockfiles: the merged `pyproject.toml`s are identical to 0.10.0's, but
    0.10.0's root `uv.lock` records 3 226 `pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com`
    sources (the README forbids committing them; CI's public runners cannot
    resolve them) and `uv lock --check` reported both locks stale. Both were
    regenerated with `uv lock` — which on this machine resolves through its
    configured mirror (`~/.config/uv/uv.toml`: `pypi-proxy.cloud.databricks.com`)
    — and then rewritten to the public hosts (`files.pythonhosted.org/packages/…`
    artifacts, `registry = "https://pypi.org/simple"`), the procedure 0.10.0's
    own changelog describes: the mirror keeps PyPI's paths and hashes, so the
    rewrite is mechanical. Every package version is unchanged against 0.10.0's
    locks (only `source` / artifact URLs differ) and no proxy host remains.
    Lesson recorded: a lock regenerated on a developer machine must be checked
    for its `url =` hosts before it is committed or deployed — the first
    rebuilt deployment shipped mirror URLs, and the Apps builder then fetched
    them literally.
11. Test seams of the merge: `tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py`
    constructs `FlatStore`; `tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py`
    expects the `sql` scope alone (their #218 rationale); the type-filter test
    in `tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py` patches their
    `TwinGraphAccess.graph_query_table` (the resolver the route now uses); the
    `_FakeStore` / `MagicMock(spec=…)` store doubles gain `record_inferred`;
    `_companion_ddl.drop_view` drops the `_asserted` companion only for a
    graph's union view — a simulation union (`__smu_`) has none (their
    `test_simulation_union_drop_all_drops_overlay_view`).
12. app.yaml.template / scripts/deploy.config.sh — the five realtime values
    (`ONTOBRICKS_REALTIME_ENABLED`, `_JOB_NAME`, `_LAKEBASE_USER`,
    `_LAKEBASE_SECRET`, `_CHECKPOINT_ROOT`) were hard-coded in the template
    (`"false"` / `""`), so every re-render of `app.yaml` switched a streaming
    deployment off — the sandbox deployment had to be edited by hand. They now
    render from `APP_REALTIME_*` (defaults `false` / empty in the deploy
    config; the empty ones are optional entries the renderer strips), as the
    instance ids already do in 0.10.0. docs/incremental-materialization.md
    says so in the Realtime deployment paragraph.

Modified files: see `git show --stat` of the merge commit (the 36 conflicted
files, the 23 rename-swept files, the boundary refactor files, the new
`src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLSQLBuiltinFilters.py`, this log).

Test result: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" -o faulthandler_timeout=240`
on the merged tree — 11796 passed, 335 skipped, 9 deselected; `uv lock --check`
clean for both lockfiles; `tests/units/architecture` 11 passed (both boundary
tests included).

================================================================================
## Rebuilt apps redeployed to the `ontobricks-rtm` sandbox; `.isaac/` excluded from the bundle sync
================================================================================

Context: the merged tree was deployed to the sandbox (`scripts/deploy.sh
--no-bootstrap`, realtime env from `APP_REALTIME_*`, their `sql`-only scopes
accepted by the Apps API as recorded). Three platform-side findings on the way:

1. The first deployment's build failed: the Apps PyPI mirror
   (`pypi-proxy.cloud.databricks.com`) answered 404 for the
   `pyasn1-0.6.5-py3-none-any.whl` path 0.10.0's floor pins (a day-old
   release); minutes later the mirror listed and served the same path (200),
   so this is the mirror's first fetch of a fresh wheel, not the lockfile — a
   retry is the remedy. Every other locked version was present on the mirror
   (scripted check of all 236).
2. The retry's deployment sat in "Preparing source code for new app
   deployment" for over 80 minutes (today's earlier deploys took ~3 min);
   `databricks bundle run` gave up at its fixed 20-minute wait while the
   deployment stayed `IN_PROGRESS` server-side. `databricks apps stop` cleared
   it (pending and active deployments reset), `apps start` + a fresh deploy
   followed.
3. databricks.yml / .databricksignore — the untracked local `.isaac/` directory
   was part of the uploaded bundle (small, harmless, but it must never ship):
   added to `sync.exclude` and to the human mirror.
4. The restarted deployment hung the same way (another hour in "Preparing
   source code" with no platform log line after "Starting Databricks Apps
   runtime"), while the MCP app redeployed from the same bundle in minutes and
   the shipped tree is the pre-merge size (14.5 MB): the app's deployment
   pipeline was wedged since its failed build. The app was deleted and
   recreated by the bundle (new service principal: self `CAN_MANAGE`, the UC
   catalog grant and the Lakebase schema grants replayed by hand, as the first
   deploy's `--no-bootstrap` path required).
4b. Recreating the app deletes its service principal, which owned the slot
    pipelines the app had created: the next `bundle deploy` renders the
    published realtime domain's pipeline (`ontobricks-slots-zzrealtimelive-v1`)
    and its `PUT /api/2.0/pipelines/<id>` fails with "Unable to access
    workspace-bound securable because the user is not assigned to the
    associated workspace" (the pipeline's creator / run-as is gone). Remedy:
    delete the orphaned pipelines and their streaming tables (`_slots`, owned by
    the pipeline) plus the domain's `_data` / `_graph`; the next build or bundle
    deploy recreates them under the new identity. Worth a `scripts/bootstrap`
    step if apps are recreated routinely.
4d. The graph objects the old service principal created in Unity Catalog (the
    gateway VIEW, `_data`, `_inferred`, companions) stay owned by the deleted
    principal, and a `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` over one of them by the new app
    fails with "does not have MANAGE on Table …": `MANAGE` is not part of
    `ALL PRIVILEGES`. `GRANT MANAGE ON CATALOG ontobricks_rtm_catalog TO
    <new sp>` (inherited by every schema and object) is the remedy; the
    `app-permissions` bootstrap should grant it alongside `ALL PRIVILEGES`.
4c. `src/mcp-server/app.yaml` is tracked (0.10.0 commits the `10x` render) and
    `scripts/deploy.sh` re-renders it on every deploy: a sandbox deploy leaves
    it modified with the sandbox's URL / warehouse / registry values — restore
    it (`git checkout src/mcp-server/app.yaml`) before committing.
5. scripts/deploy.config.sh — `DEFAULT_LAKEBASE_DATABASE` and
   `DEFAULT_LAKEBASE_SCHEMA` take an environment override like the instance id
   does (0.10.0 moved the defaults to `ontobricks_demo_10_*`; the sandbox
   registry lives in the `09` database and schema, and the first rebuilt deploy
   had silently created an empty `ontobricks_demo_10_registry_db` on the
   project — deleted again).

Modified files:
- databricks.yml
- .databricksignore
- scripts/deploy.config.sh
- docs/deployment.md (the two Lakebase defaults are env-overridable)
- uv.lock, src/mcp-server/uv.lock (public hosts, see item 10 above)
- changelogs/v0.10.0/dermot-smyth_2026-11-04.log

Deploy result (2026-11-04, `ontobricks-rtm`): both apps RUNNING on the merged
tree, `/health` → version 0.10.0; the rebuilt app sees the `09` registry (the
three `Zz*` domains), loads the published realtime domain and answers
`realtime: {enabled: true, source_configured: true, kind: kafka}` with
`decision.effective: realtime`; scenario 06 PASSED in 228 s — readiness
`row_tracking_missing → full`, enable-row-tracking → `incremental`, the
Domain › Backend card ("incremental runs as incremental · Mappings: 2
row-local …"), an incremental build of 6 triples in 179.7 s (`strategy: mv`,
no fallback, slot pipeline created under the new identity), status, build-run
facts, the overview (`domains_per_mode: {incremental: 1, microbatch: 1}`) and
the Knowledge Graph › Build status card ("Slot pipeline: IDLE · _data: mv ·
_slots: streaming_table v5 · … 6 upserted, 0 deleted"). Screenshots in
`artifacts/scenarios/` (git-ignored).
